<TextPage title="Private AI chat: uncensored models that don't log you" description="Which uncensored AI chat platforms offer private, anonymized, or end-to-end encrypted conversations? A comparison of privacy policies and logging behavior." kicker="Feature comparison">
  <div class="empty-state"><strong>Live benchmark pending.</strong><p>Privacy scores publish after provider policy review is complete. This page remains noindex until then.</p></div>
  <h2>Privacy is not a checkbox</h2>
  <p>"We don't sell your data" is not the same as "we don't store your data." "End-to-end encrypted" is not the same as "anonymized." And none of these are the same as "your conversations are used to train the next model."</p>
  <p>For uncensored chat, privacy matters more — the conversations are sensitive by nature, and a data breach or policy change can expose content the user reasonably expected to remain private.</p>
  <h2>Privacy tiers we test</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>End-to-end encrypted (E2EE):</strong> The provider cannot read your messages. Venice offers E2EE routes for select models. This is the gold standard.</li>
    <li><strong>Private / no-logging:</strong> The provider states it does not retain conversation history or use it for training. We verify this against the published privacy policy and API metadata.</li>
    <li><strong>Anonymized:</strong> The provider logs conversations but strips identifiable metadata. Risk level: moderate.</li>
    <li><strong>Logged / training-enabled:</strong> Conversations may be reviewed by humans or used for model improvement. Risk level: high for sensitive content.</li>
    <li><strong>Unknown:</strong> The provider's policy is ambiguous, contradictory, or absent. Treated as logged until proven otherwise.</li>
  </ol>
  <h2>What we verify (not just what the policy says)</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Published privacy policy and data-retention terms.</li>
    <li>API response metadata: does the provider return flags indicating logging or training use?</li>
    <li>Deletion process: can you request and confirm deletion of your conversation history?</li>
    <li>Training-use opt-out: is there a documented route to exclude your data from training?</li>
    <li>Jurisdiction and subprocessor disclosure.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Models with strong privacy characteristics</h2>
  <p>Venice's E2EE routes (Gemma 4 Uncensored, Qwen 3 Uncensored-P) are the current privacy leaders for uncensored chat. Local models run through Ollama or similar tools offer complete privacy but require self-hosted hardware. OpenRouter routes vary by underlying provider — the OpenRouter privacy policy applies, but the upstream model provider's policy may also be relevant.</p>
